A successful "data from" rule combined with a showdata action should result in
a new buffer being opened in the editor with the new data.

-- config --
path: tests/data/config/without-fsys.toml
-- plumbing-rules --
data matches load-me
data from echo "some synthesised data"
attr add action=showdata filename=+testing
plumb to edit
-- file-load-me.txt --
load-me
-- actions --
type: x\n
-- buffer-list --
1      load-me.txt
2    * +testing
-- expected-windows --
2
-- expected-buffer-2 --
some synthesised data
